{"name":"Cabbage Rose","hex":"#c59f91","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cabbage rose","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A plant of a hybrid rose species with large numbers of petals, Rosa × centifolia.","The fragrant flower of such a plant."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cabbage_rose"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rosa × centifolia","blocks":[{"text":"Rosa × centifolia, the Provence rose, cabbage rose, May rose or Rose de Mai, is a hybrid rose developed by Dutch breeders in the period between the 17th century and the 19th century, possibly earlier."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Rosa_centifolia_foliacea_17.jpg/330px-Rosa_centifolia_foliacea_17.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rosa_%C3%97_centifolia","wikidata":"Q640505"},{"title":"Cabbage","blocks":[{"text":"Cabbage, comprising several cultivars of Brassica oleracea, is a leafy green, red (purple), or white biennial plant grown as an annual vegetable crop for its dense-leaved heads. It is descended from the wild cabbage, and belongs to the \"cole crops\" or brassicas, meaning it is closely related to broccoli and cauliflower ; Brussels sprouts ; and Savoy cabbage."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Cabbage_and_cross_section_on_white.jpg/330px-Cabbage_and_cross_section_on_white.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cabbage","wikidata":"Q35051"},{"title":"Rose","blocks":[{"text":"A rose is either a woody perennial flowering plant of the genus Rosa, in the family Rosaceae, or the flower it bears. There are over three hundred species and tens of thousands of cultivars. The plants range in size and form, from trailing and erect shrubs to climbers up to 7 metres (23 ft) in height. Sharp prickles appear on the stems of many species. Their flowers vary in size and shape and are usually large and showy, in colours ranging from white through pinks, reds, oranges and yellows."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Rosa_rubiginosa_1.jpg/330px-Rosa_rubiginosa_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rose","wikidata":"Q34687"},{"title":"Rose (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Rose is the color halfway between red and magenta, whose hue corresponds to an angle of 330 degrees on the HSV/HSL color wheel."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Pink-Rose-Sitia-Crete.jpg/330px-Pink-Rose-Sitia-Crete.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rose_(color)","wikidata":"Q533047"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Rosa_Gloire_des_Mousseux_2.jpg/500px-Rosa_Gloire_des_Mousseux_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/32/Rosa_Gloire_des_Mousseux_2.jpg/500px-Rosa_Gloire_des_Mousseux_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"\"Moss\" on the bud of a centifolia moss rose","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARosa_Gloire_des_Mousseux_2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Rosa_centifolia_foliacea.jpg/500px-Rosa_centifolia_foliacea.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Rosa_centifolia_foliacea.jpg/1280px-Rosa_centifolia_foliacea.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/Rosa_centifolia_foliacea.jpg/500px-Rosa_centifolia_foliacea.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"a blooming flower of Rosa ce